        System.out.println(containsDuplicate(nums));
    }
}


happy number

import java.util.HashSet;

public class HappyNumber {

    public static boolean isHappy(int n) {

        HashSet<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();

        while(n != 1) {

            // Cycle check
            if(set.contains(n)) {
                return false;
            }

            // Store visited number
            set.add(n);

            n = getSum(n);
        }

        return true;
    }


    public static int getSum(int n) {

        int sum = 0;

        while(n > 0) {

            int digit = n % 10;

            sum = sum + digit * digit;

            n = n / 10;
        }

        return sum;
    }


    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int n = 19;

        System.out.println(isHappy(n));
    }
}


Heap

Heap is a special type of Binary Tree data structure.

It is a complete binary tree where every parent node follows a special rule.


Minimum value quickly 
Maximum value quickly 


Types of Heap
1. Max Heap

Rule:

Parent value is greater than children.

Example:

          100
        /     \
      50       70
     /
   20

Check:

100 > 50
100 > 70
50 > 20

Correct.

2. Min Heap

Rule:

Parent value is smaller than children.

Example:

          10
        /    \
      20      30
     /
   40

Check:

10 < 20
10 < 30
20 < 40

Correct.


Max Heap Operations

Operations:

Insert → Heapify Up
Delete Root → Heapify Down
Get Maximum → Peek
